  "worked_solution": "Note that we can write the given probability as\n\n$$\nP(\\mu -4\\mu <X<\\mu +4\\mu )=0.6476,\n$$\n\nwhich tells us that the interval $-3\\mu <X<5\\mu $ is symmetric about the mean $\\mu .$\n\nFirst, we find the cumulative probability using symmetry:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(\\mu -4\\mu <X<\\mu +4\\mu ) & =0.6476 \\\\ 2P(\\mu <X<\\mu +4\\mu ) & =0.6476 \\\\ P(\\mu <X<\\mu +4\\mu ) & =0.3238 \\\\ P(X<\\mu +4\\mu )-P(X<\\mu ) & =0.3238 \\\\ P(X<\\mu +4\\mu )-0.5 & =0.3238 \\\\ P(X<\\mu +4\\mu ) & =0.8238 \\\\ P(X\\le \\mu +4\\mu ) & =0.8238 \\\\ P(X\\le 5\\mu ) & =0.8238\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we transform to a standard normal random variable by $z$-scoring:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\le 5\\mu ) & =0.8238 \\\\ P(Z\\le \\frac{5\\mu -\\mu }{7}) & =0.8238 \\\\ \u03a6(\\frac{4\\mu }{7}) & =0.8238 \\\\ \\frac{4\\mu }{7} & ={\u03a6}^{-1}(0.8238)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nAccording to the table, we have\n\n$$\n\u03a6(0.93)=0.8238\\,\u21d2\\,{\u03a6}^{-1}(0.8238)=0.93.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{4\\mu }{7} & =0.93 \\\\ 4\\mu  & =6.51 \\\\ \\mu  & =\\frac{6.51}{4} \\\\ \\mu  & \u22481.63.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to $2$ decimal places.",
